  "details": "# Issue:\n\nWhen selecting Users in Desktop using the \"Select User\" Quick Menu Button you will get a popup saying \"Interaction mode set to Direct Touch\".\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n\n1. Start VRChat in Desktop Mode\n\n2. Go to an instance with other users\n\n3. Open your Quick Menu\n\n4. Click on the \"Select User\" Quick Action\n\n5. Now click on another user in your Instance\n\nIf you do this you will notice a \"Interaction mode set to Direct Touch\" popup at the bottom of the Quick Menu.\n\n# Expected Behaviour:\n\nFrom what it looks like this popup is normally expected to show for Android Users using a touchscreen, so I would only expect this popup to show up there and not for Desktop users.\n\n# Attachments:\n\nHere is a video showcasing the issue:\n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/07g095.mp4\n\nHere is a picture showcasing the issue:",
